1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,680
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:04,617
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,237
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,496
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,995
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,440
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,640
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,080
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:24,257
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,697
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:29,537
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:34,980
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:40,380
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for!

14
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:52,617
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:58,437
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,117
That legendary place.

18
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,837
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:06,697
Is only legendary?

20
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:10,137
Till someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:12,577
Through it all.

22
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,457
Through all the trouble of times.

23
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:15,717
Through the heartache.

24
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:16,837
And through the pain.

25
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:19,577
Know that I will be there.

26
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,337
To stand by you.

27
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:24,260
Like I know you'll stand by me.

28
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:26,817
So come aboard!

29
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:30,720
And bring along all your hopes and dreams.

30
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:36,040
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

31
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,717
There's always room for you.

32
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,540
If you wanna be my friend?

33
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,720
We are, we are on the crew.

34
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:49,740
We are.

35
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,820
You just never learn, do you? Let's go!

36
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,238
I'll pay you later!

37
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:02,960
Any way you want.

38
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:05,437
You made a boy cry?

39
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:06,700
He made me mad.

40
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,040
Oh, it's okay.

41
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:09,580
Kids won't be kids.

42
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:13,080
He said your tangerine
sucks. He what? Bellamere!

43
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:15,880
Never give up.

44
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:22,140
You must find the strength
inside you to always move on.

45
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:26,480
You must live through every moment.

46
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:36,760
And if you can smile in the face of
it all that is the greatest dream

47
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:52,240
while I'm in charge those without money
will die now do you understand me you worms

48
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,277
what's this?

49
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,537
That's my map!

50
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:02,502
I drew it and you can't have it!

51
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,800
A child drew this?

52
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:06,540
Give it back! No!

53
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:08,370
Huh.

54
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:11,040
Very good.

55
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,600
She could be useful.

56
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,760
Bring her with us. Right?

57
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,310
No!

58
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:19,730
No!

59
00:03:19,813 --> 00:03:20,860
Why did I go?

60
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,412
Why did I go to trouble?

61
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:25,640
You promised not to hurt
her if you got your money.

62
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:27,370
Right.

63
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:28,520
I won't hurt you.

64
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:30,037
Just borrow her for a while.

65
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:31,400
Genzo, help me!

66
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:34,160
I won't let you take her! Karumi.

67
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:40,370
Genzo!

68
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,180
Genzo, get her!

69
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:44,510
Genzo!

70
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:52,400
I'll save you, Nami.

71
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:55,020
I won't let you go.

72
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:56,580
No, please!

73
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:59,320
It's okay, you don't need to save me!

74
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:01,060
Enough of this!

75
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:02,460
I will save you!

76
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,700
Please, no more killing!

77
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:20,500
All of our ships have been sunk.

78
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:27,940
I'm afraid our plan to have Nami and
Nojiko escape to the sea was a bad plan.

79
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:31,309
The Marines won't bother
trying to save us.

80
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,860
We've lost our island.

81
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:35,875
Bellamere knew that this would happen.

82
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:40,864
Her experiences in the Marines taught her
what all these creatures are capable of.

83
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:43,580
She knew that none of us would escape.

84
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,460
They've taken Nami!

85
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,560
What am I supposed to do now?

86
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:55,530
Bellamy!

87
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:02,220
We know where Arlong and his crew are.

88
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:05,837
It looks like they're going to
settle right here on this island.

89
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,337
It's time to decide.

90
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:09,517
We can fight to the death right now,

91
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,877
or we can take a chance that the
Marines will someday come to save us?

92
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:15,417
and hope and pray we don't
get killed before then.

93
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:16,540
Your choice!

94
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:20,036
Only Marine Headquarters
stands a chance against them.

95
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:23,577
But they have their hands
full with the Grand Line.

96
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:28,237
The chances that they would come all the
way out here for us are as good as zero.

97
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,940
But I can't just sit
here and abandon Nami.

98
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:32,960
We must fight!

99
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:36,730
I'm in.

100
00:05:36,813 --> 00:05:40,337
I can't just stand by and do
nothing when a child is in danger.

101
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:42,417
Now who else will come fight beside us?

102
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:43,380
I don't care.

103
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:44,370
Do you kill me?

104
00:05:44,453 --> 00:05:45,577
I'm going to save that little brat.

105
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:46,897
Tell him your favorite life.

106
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:47,810
You can't quit now.

107
00:05:47,893 --> 00:05:48,723
We should do no less.

108
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:49,636
Let's fight!

109
00:05:49,719 --> 00:05:51,977
It's just one of us fights,
they'll blame us all.

110
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:52,942
So let's do it!

111
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,360
Nami! Nami!

112
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:04,900
Nami! What? You're okay!

113
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,400
Nami! Nami!

114
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,010
Everyone look!

115
00:06:09,093 --> 00:06:09,923
Are you okay?

116
00:06:10,006 --> 00:06:11,294
Did they hurt you any?

117
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:15,410
Hey!

118
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,460
I'm joining you.

119
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:19,210
Huh?

120
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:23,820
I'm joining Arlong's crew!

121
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:27,160
I'll get to be a navigator and draw maps.

122
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:33,700
What in the world are you talking about?

123
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:39,020
Stand back Did they threaten to
do something terrible to you?

124
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:41,317
Please, tell me. No.

125
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,977
They must have done something.

126
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:43,917
No, no.

127
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:44,877
Tell the truth.

128
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:47,080
Let go of me. Nami?

129
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:58,540
But that's an Arlong tattoo, not you. Why?

130
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:01,420
Look at this.

131
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:04,160
They gave me all this money.

132
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:11,120
They say, don't buy me
anything I want. No!

133
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:14,011
I will never forgive you if you join them.

134
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,070
Don't you understand?

135
00:07:15,153 --> 00:07:17,380
They killed Bellemere in front of us!

136
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:19,051
She died to keep us safe!

137
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:21,060
I'll never forgive you! Never!

138
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,517
You're not my sister!

139
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,430
Who cares?

140
00:07:23,513 --> 00:07:26,437
Why would I want to live like
Bellemere if it just gets you killed?

141
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,340
I don't want to die like that!

142
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:32,720
How could you?

143
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:34,830
Bellemere?

144
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:40,217
Bellemere gave her life so that you
and I could go on living together!

145
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,594
That's enough, Nojiko.

146
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,717
Leave us, Nami!

147
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:46,320
Never set foot in this village again.

148
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:54,960
Help me!

149
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:01,080
I don't understand.

150
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:04,071
How could she betray her family like that?

151
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,540
For money?

152
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:08,300
Bellamy was like her mother.

153
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:20,280
Nami loved Bellamere.

154
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:22,380
I know she did.

155
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,700
Hey, didn't Bellamere always say?

156
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:38,217
Good things will come your way!

157
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,980
as long as you continue to live?

158
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,460
Lots of good things.

159
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:45,950
Yes.

160
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:52,520
After Arlong took me, I watched him sink
five marine ships like they were toys.

161
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:55,040
I don't think they'll send anymore.

162
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:56,820
We're on our own.

163
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:59,880
So I decided I'd do something about it.

164
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:04,157
I made a deal with Arlong to
buy Cocoyashi Village from...

165
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:06,520
Buy Cocoyashi? How?

166
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:09,580
For a hundred million berries.

167
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:15,060
If I buy the town, we'll be free.

168
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,180
No one else will die.

169
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:21,160
And all I have to do is
join his crew and draw maps.

170
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:23,145
But a hundred million berries?

171
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:25,757
You can't earn that
working your whole life!

172
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:28,016
I will get that money no matter what!

173
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:31,777
People are having a hard enough
time paying their own tribute.

174
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:33,680
So I have to do this alone.

175
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:37,661
If anyone tries to help
me, they'll just get hurt.

176
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:45,417
Won't it be hard?

177
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:49,957
Yeah, living with the people
who killed our mother.

178
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,557
I'll be okay.

179
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:55,237
I'll just smile every time I see his face.

180
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:57,077
I'm not gonna cry anymore.

181
00:09:57,160 --> 00:10:03,060
I'm gonna fight by myself.

182
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:25,320
To make a choice like that
when you're only ten years old?

183
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:28,032
Do you know how hard that must have been?

184
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:32,460
All to save the village she loves so much.

185
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:34,397
That girl...

186
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:38,220
Whoever makes Nami suffer
is going to hear from me!

187
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:41,240
Oh, why'd you do that?

188
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,800
Because I'm telling you to stay out of it.

189
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:47,637
If you go around saying
that she's your friend,

190
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,917
they're going to become suspicious of her.

191
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,137
Then her eight years of suffering
will have been for nothing.

192
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:55,720
Don't make it harder than it already is.

193
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:58,020
She has to fight alone.

194
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:02,911
Knowing there are people who call her
friend only makes the suffering worse.

195
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:26,957
A pirate thief that's right
the only thing this place

196
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:29,597
has going for it is plenty
of pirates to steal from

197
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:35,117
i'm gonna make them pay
you're all cut up yeah i kind

198
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:39,560
of screwed up but look one
million Who cares about that?

199
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:40,759
You need a doctor!

200
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:41,730
It's nothing.

201
00:11:41,813 --> 00:11:43,093
These cups are nothing.

202
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:45,360
No one will find it here.

203
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:48,380
I'll save up, little by little.

204
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:52,260
By the time this is filled,
I'll have my hundred million.

205
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:56,360
Still a long way to go.

206
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:00,440
One hundred million berries.

207
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:06,620
It's taken a while, but
only seven million left.

208
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:11,257
I can get that with one more job.

209
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:13,157
Just one more trip!

210
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,005
And this will finally be over.

211
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,980
Arlong's rule will be over.

212
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:20,804
Cocoyashi Village will be free.

213
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,720
I will be free.

214
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,320
And then?

215
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:29,920
And then I think I'll finally be
able to smile again. For real!

216
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,150
Bellamere.

217
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:51,900
So why do the marines want Nami?

218
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:56,300
Your job is to lead the way quietly.

219
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,857
A hat pinwheel.

220
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:03,040
Where in the world did he get that?

221
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:05,000
It's so cool!

222
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,080
One more little job.

223
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:15,574
Well, let's get to it.

224
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:21,570
Enies?

225
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:22,740
And the Marines?

226
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,180
Are you the pirate thief known as Name?

227
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:34,837
The marine sources have
revealed that you have quite a

228
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:37,717
large sum of treasure that
you've stolen from pirates.

229
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:40,537
The government hereby confiscates
everything you've stolen.

230
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:42,697
It is required that
you comply immediately.

231
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:43,839
Do you understand?

232
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,417
I'm only going to warn you once.

233
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:50,147
I'm one of the leaders
of the Arlong Pirates.

234
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:53,162
If you mess with me, Arlong
won't sit by quietly.

235
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:55,380
Silly girl.

236
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:56,797
Who do you think I am?

237
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:59,468
Do you honestly think
you can intimidate me?

238
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:01,280
Find the stolen goods!

239
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:04,160
Don't move!

240
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:11,720
I said stop!

241
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:20,117
Do you really think this is what
the Marines should be doing now?

242
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,097
The Arlong pirates are murderers.

243
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:25,457
They've destroyed entire cities
and you're doing nothing!

244
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:29,246
He's ruling over this island and
trampling over people's lives.

245
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:33,437
You'd ignore Arlong's atrocities
to steal from a thief?

246
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:35,108
Is that what you stand for?

247
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,820
Big talk from a filthy criminal.

248
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:39,931
Continue the search, man.

249
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,097
Every person on this
island has been waiting

250
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:44,757
for the Marines to come
and help them for years.

251
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:48,257
How dare you pass them by and
come here searching for money?

252
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:51,077
Colonel, this tangerine orchard
seems a little suspicious.

253
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:51,990
Dig it up.

254
00:14:52,073 --> 00:14:53,900
The whole thing, if need be.

255
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:59,293
Keep your filthy hands off
Bellamere's Tangerine Orchard!

256
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:04,340
I won't let you take my money!

257
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:05,717
That money's for...

258
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:06,900
it's for...

259
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:12,440
That poor girl's money is meant
to save Pokayashi Village.

260
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:16,920
What gives you the right to take our
salvation away from her? Damn you!

261
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:19,740
My, my.

262
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:23,257
A mere village representative
talking down to a marine colonel.

263
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:24,170
How bold.

264
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:27,840
Genzo, how'd you know about that?

265
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:34,020
I've always known, Nami.

266
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:38,440
I couldn't believe what you had done.

267
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:41,640
So I confronted Nojiko about it later.

268
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:43,170
Since then,

269
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:45,517
everyone has known that
you stayed with the

270
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:48,541
Arlong pirates so that you
could save the village.

271
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:51,617
But we all agreed we'd
never tell you that we knew.

272
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:55,097
If you ever thought the villagers
were placing their hopes on you,

273
00:15:55,180 --> 00:15:58,317
you might never leave his gang
for fear of letting us down?

274
00:15:58,400 --> 00:15:59,980
That can't be!

275
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,137
Now hold on a minute, just what
are you trying to say here?

276
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:07,957
Are you telling me that the villagers are

277
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:10,557
thieves and we should
arrest every one of them?

278
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:11,837
Is that what you're saying?

279
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:15,977
What he's saying is that every last
one of us is fighting to survive.

280
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:18,537
We have to fend for
ourselves because we can't

281
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:20,577
rely on support from
you government people!

282
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:24,917
So, if you're not going to protect our
village, then get the hell out of here.

283
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,440
And be quick about it, or
Arlong will sink your ship, too.

284
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,450
Arlong will.

285
00:16:30,533 --> 00:16:32,140
I wouldn't be so sure.

286
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:36,020
You still haven't found it?

287
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:40,378
We're looking for a hundred million
berries here, not a grain of rice!

288
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:41,800
Hey, you!

289
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:44,100
How do you know how much there is?

290
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,697
Oh, I don't know.

291
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:51,368
I just have a hunch that that's
the amount we're looking for.

292
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:03,390
It's him.

293
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:09,890
Tell me!

294
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:12,374
It was Erlong that sent you, wasn't it?

295
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:14,420
Of course not.

296
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,557
I wouldn't do a pirate's dirty work.

297
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:17,470
That'd be wrong.

298
00:17:17,553 --> 00:17:21,737
I'm just a public servant dealing with
theft the way any government worker would.

299
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:24,120
You corrupt marine scumbag!

300
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:27,653
The marine comes due to being
nothing but pirate cronies!

301
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:30,270
Arlong!

302
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:32,500
Sir, I found it!

303
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:42,210
Incredible.

304
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:46,049
I must say I'm impressed you've
gathered this much treasure.

305
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:50,200
The money's all ragged and
bloody. No matter. Money's money.

306
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:56,280
30 % of this is all mine.

307
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:58,300
Don't touch that.

308
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:00,520
Don't touch that.

309
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:03,380
Don't touch that. Nami!

310
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:05,400
Stop it!

311
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:06,600
Don't touch that!

312
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:08,120
Stop it!

313
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:25,657
No! No! No!

314
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:26,820
No! No!

315
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,280
No!

316
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:32,170
Nojiko!

317
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:34,170
Nojiko!

318
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:41,100
Doctor! Doctor!

319
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,777
Genzo, what is it?

320
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:46,300
Nojiko's been shot. By who?

321
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:48,800
The Marines. The Marines?

322
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:55,390
Nami?

323
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,320
Hey, Nami!

324
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:58,640
What's up?

325
00:18:58,740 --> 00:19:00,152
Need help with anything?

326
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:04,080
Why are you still here?

327
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:06,480
Stay out of my business!

328
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:08,585
Just get away from our island!

329
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:16,910
Arlong!

330
00:19:16,993 --> 00:19:18,273
I bet it's the village.

331
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:19,980
You want it left alone.

332
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:21,670
Arlong!

333
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:24,780
Gather up 100 million
berries, then bring it to me.

334
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:29,317
Do so and I will let your village go,
in addition to giving you your freedom.

335
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:30,230
Arlong!

336
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:32,437
And I'm the kind of fish
man who would rather

337
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:35,037
die than break an
agreement concerning money.

338
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:37,377
And I don't even care
how long it takes you.

339
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:39,048
I will honor our agreement.

340
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,230
Arlong!

341
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:47,060
What's her problem?

342
00:19:49,780 --> 00:19:50,610
Arlong!

343
00:19:51,860 --> 00:19:52,760
Hmm? Hmm?

344
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:57,740
Ah, what seems to be the problem,
oh skilled surveyor of ours?

345
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,240
Why the sour face?

346
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:04,920
Those marine maggots you keep on the
payroll stole every last berry I had.

347
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:08,757
What happened to all that crap about
dying before you'd ever break a promise?

348
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:10,722
when it comes to money, bastard?

349
00:20:11,020 --> 00:20:12,260
Refresh my memory.

350
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:13,397
Did I break a promise?

351
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,757
Don't play dumb with me!

352
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:17,546
I know that you've teamed
up with the Marines!

353
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:20,600
Just when did I break that promise?

354
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:22,120
Speak up, girl.

355
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,190
Damn.

356
00:20:32,273 --> 00:20:33,840
Damn you. Damn you!

357
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,070
Too bad.

358
00:20:37,153 --> 00:20:39,041
All your stolen money got stolen.

359
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:41,257
That certainly is unfortunate.

360
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:43,560
But a deal is a deal, Nami.

361
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:46,517
If you can't come up
with 100 million berries,

362
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:49,957
then both you and your village
stay in my possession indefinitely.

363
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,800
Well, you know the terms.

364
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:53,540
You pig!

365
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:58,660
It's only 100 million berries.

366
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:01,702
Start saving again and
you'll have it in no time.

367
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:06,940
Or are you gonna run out on me?

368
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:13,720
Listen, if you do that, I'll kill everyone
in that village Do you understand me?

369
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:21,000
Nami, we agreed we would
never tell you that we knew.

370
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:23,977
If you thought all of
us were counting on you?

371
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:28,766
You would be bound by guilt never to leave
his gang for fear of letting us down.

372
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:36,220
Ah, running away so soon!

373
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:41,557
Shouldn't we chase after her?

374
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:43,077
No need for that.

375
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:45,037
Trust me, Hachi.

376
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:46,557
She's not going anywhere.

377
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:51,040
There's no way Nami could just abandon
the lives of all those villagers.

378
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:54,677
Now that's what I call playing dirty.

379
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:59,020
There's no way I'd let go of
an asset like Nami that easily.

380
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:02,680
I may be cruel, but I'm
not totally heartless.

381
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:08,740
Once she's done charting all the
world's oceans, she'll have her freedom.

382
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,051
That's pretty harsh, man.

383
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:14,827
It'll take decades for sure.

384
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:18,475
Yeah, it's been a hundred
years, wouldn't it be enough?

385
00:22:26,860 --> 00:22:28,737
We've had enough. Take up arms.

386
00:22:28,820 --> 00:22:29,938
It's time to fight!

387
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:37,300
Genzo, please don't do anything stupid!

388
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:41,360
We have to live or our
struggles will mean nothing!

389
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:44,702
You can't throw your lives away!

390
00:22:45,260 --> 00:22:50,240
Eight long years ago, we promised
we wouldn't live our lives in vain.

391
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:54,377
No matter the pain or humiliation
we endured under Arlong,

392
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:58,640
We swore to fight the long fight
so Nami could meet their demands.

393
00:22:58,940 --> 00:23:00,100
But they lied.

394
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:03,197
They never intended to
keep their end of the deal.

395
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:06,045
Instead, they stole our
only chance at freedom.

396
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:07,270
So now,

397
00:23:07,353 --> 00:23:09,957
we should make those
filthy fishmen pay for

398
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:12,337
the years they manipulated
that kind young girl.

399
00:23:12,420 --> 00:23:13,250
Am I right?

400
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:15,040
Yeah, let's do this.

401
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:17,677
We were always ready to
fight those monsters.

402
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:18,642
Let's get them.

403
00:23:19,060 --> 00:23:22,707
Time to show those lousy, stinking
fishmen what we're made of.

404
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,230
Yeah!

405
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:25,620
Everybody, wait!

406
00:23:26,380 --> 00:23:27,210
Huh?

407
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:28,670
Nami.

408
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,360
Calm down.

409
00:23:33,700 --> 00:23:35,260
It's not that much money.

410
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:37,325
I can make it back in no time.

411
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:38,537
I'll take care of it.

412
00:23:38,620 --> 00:23:39,450
Don't worry.

413
00:23:39,820 --> 00:23:41,920
It'll be easy this time.

414
00:23:42,120 --> 00:23:43,137
I'm used to it.

415
00:23:43,220 --> 00:23:44,820
I'll be fine. Just relax.

416
00:23:45,040 --> 00:23:46,158
Everything is okay.

417
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:49,580
Hey, it's nothing compared to back then.

418
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:52,380
It's okay.

419
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:54,089
You don't need to save me.

420
00:23:54,460 --> 00:23:55,920
Come on, everyone.

421
00:23:56,220 --> 00:23:57,540
I'm perfectly fine.

422
00:24:03,780 --> 00:24:05,080
You've done enough.

423
00:24:05,340 --> 00:24:07,928
You have to know that
there is no point now.

424
00:24:08,260 --> 00:24:12,680
You struggled so hard carrying our
lives on your back this whole time.

425
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:15,737
I can only imagine that
joining them must have been

426
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:18,761
more painful than being
stabbed through the heart.

427
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:21,760
You fought very well.

428
00:24:23,980 --> 00:24:24,810
Genzo?

429
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:33,400
Set yourself free from this village

430
00:24:34,940 --> 00:24:35,770
Genzo?

431
00:24:36,900 --> 00:24:39,720
Nami, do it! What? Nojiko!

432
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:42,040
Nami... Go on.

433
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:45,377
You're an exceptional young woman!

434
00:24:45,460 --> 00:24:46,637
And you have a dream?

435
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:48,520
Everyone, listen!

436
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:51,040
I won't let you go!

437
00:24:52,180 --> 00:24:53,640
Just stay right there!

438
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:57,409
I'm not going to let anyone
else get hurt by these monsters!

439
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:00,880
You'll all die.

440
00:25:01,620 --> 00:25:02,760
We know that.

441
00:25:09,060 --> 00:25:10,600
Nami, it's no use.

442
00:25:10,780 --> 00:25:12,192
We've made up our minds.

443
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:17,420
Get out of the way!

444
00:25:19,980 --> 00:25:20,960
Move out!

445
00:25:21,760 --> 00:25:24,720
We may not win, but we
will give them hell!

446
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:54,420
Ha-ha-ha.

447
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:15,220
Arlug!

448
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:22,130
Luffy

449
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:27,400
What do you want?

450
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:29,457
You don't know anything about this.

451
00:26:29,540 --> 00:26:33,277
You don't know what's been happening on
this island for the past eight years.

452
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:34,660
Nope, I don't.

453
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:37,880
This has nothing to do with you.

454
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:41,177
I told you to leave this place.

455
00:26:41,260 --> 00:26:42,457
Yep, you sure did.

456
00:26:42,540 --> 00:26:43,817
So leave.

457
00:26:43,900 --> 00:26:46,000
I told you to leave!

458
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:47,380
Get out of here!

459
00:26:47,620 --> 00:26:48,796
Get out of here now!

460
00:26:50,280 --> 00:26:51,110
Go!

461
00:26:51,193 --> 00:26:53,280
Go away! Go! Go! Go!

462
00:27:08,840 --> 00:27:09,670
Luffy...

463
00:27:10,560 --> 00:27:11,760
Help me...

464
00:27:17,840 --> 00:27:19,160
Of course.

465
00:27:19,740 --> 00:27:21,520
That's what friends do.

466
00:27:23,820 --> 00:27:25,480
He's gonna pay!

467
00:27:28,900 --> 00:27:31,680
You better keep your hands off my hat!

468
00:27:33,680 --> 00:27:34,560
Luffy?

469
00:27:41,260 --> 00:27:42,440
Let's go.

470
00:27:44,120 --> 00:27:44,950
Right.

471
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:51,360
Hey, are you guys all right?

472
00:27:52,080 --> 00:27:54,160
Did Arlong do this to you?

473
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:56,360
Move aside.

474
00:27:57,980 --> 00:28:00,980
We have business to take
care of with the fishmen.

475
00:28:01,140 --> 00:28:03,917
When we finally found out the
truth about Big Sist Nami,

476
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:07,297
we realized the only thing we could
do was defeat Arlong in battle.

477
00:28:07,380 --> 00:28:10,321
So we decided to come back
here and challenge him.

478
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:12,854
Yeah, then we lost, but only by a hair.

479
00:28:14,660 --> 00:28:17,157
I'm sorry, but I can't
let you through this door.

480
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:18,937
You have no chance of victory!

481
00:28:19,020 --> 00:28:19,980
What's that?

482
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:21,030
Be patient.

483
00:28:21,113 --> 00:28:22,217
It won't be long now!

484
00:28:22,300 --> 00:28:24,537
You see, we're waiting for
the arrival of certain men.

485
00:28:24,620 --> 00:28:26,200
What certain men?

486
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:27,670
Don't worry.

487
00:28:27,753 --> 00:28:29,097
They'll be here soon!

488
00:28:29,180 --> 00:28:31,120
I'd bet my life on it.?

489
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:47,590
There!

490
00:29:03,160 --> 00:29:04,160
It's them.

491
00:29:04,580 --> 00:29:07,180
Why would they come to defend our village?

492
00:29:07,800 --> 00:29:12,397
If those men can't handle Arlong and
his gang, then there really is no hope.

493
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:15,656
Not only for this island,
but for the whole East Blue.

494
00:29:16,120 --> 00:29:20,355
Those are the faces of the four men
who are here to change your destiny.

495
00:29:20,540 --> 00:29:22,599
Earn their images into your memory.

496
00:29:31,760 --> 00:29:33,540
Step aside! Ah!

497
00:29:40,060 --> 00:29:40,890
Hey,

498
00:29:40,973 --> 00:29:42,757
do you think those two idiots that showed

499
00:29:42,840 --> 00:29:45,840
up earlier are members of
Zoro's little crew? Zoro?

500
00:29:46,100 --> 00:29:47,747
They seem too weak for that.

501
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,657
They weren't even worth killing.

502
00:29:49,740 --> 00:29:50,740
That's for sure!

503
00:30:05,040 --> 00:30:06,160
What the...

504
00:30:08,860 --> 00:30:11,020
Now, which one of you is Arlong?

505
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:44,497
As I watched the sunrise,
I began to wonder.

506
00:30:44,580 --> 00:30:49,157
What could be the reason
it's so hot inside?

507
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:55,297
No answer has come, but I can't
get away from what's true.

508
00:30:55,380 --> 00:30:57,980
It's because of you.

509
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:05,457
Show me how to catch those
feelings, get on to come back to me!

510
00:31:05,540 --> 00:31:07,777
I'll do what I must be.

511
00:31:07,860 --> 00:31:10,557
Cause they're everything I want to be.

512
00:31:10,640 --> 00:31:13,037
Pass these arms around my dreams.

513
00:31:13,120 --> 00:31:15,097
And pull them back from yesterday.

514
00:31:15,180 --> 00:31:20,520
If I'm holding hands with you,
I'm sure that we can make the way.
